     "kashikone"
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "kashinomiya-inari",
    "category": "shrine",
    "name": {
     "en": "Kashinomiya Inari Shrine",
     "ja": "柏の宮稲荷神社"
    },
    "about": {
     "en": "Built in the Meiji era as the private shrine of Kashinomiya-en, the garden estate that is now Kashinomiya Park, and moved to its present spot when the park was laid out. It sits at the top of a flight of steps, guarded by stone foxes on a base dated 1857.",
     "ja": "明治時代、現在の柏の宮公園にあった庭園「柏の宮園」の邸内社として建てられ、公園の整備で今の場所へ移された。石段の上に鎮座し、1857年銘の台座に乗る石の狐が守っている。"
    },
    "location": [
